  "cover_text": "Mahatma Gandhi1 once said, “The world provides enough for its present needs, but not for its wants.”\nIf 1 God is Infinite and Omniscient, He can subsist on His own needs. Why then does He provide for His wants, His desires?\nGandhi postulated that, for God to satisfy His requires, He must first satisfy His wants. The latter—and the matter that offers the true understanding of desires—is truth. Universe does not need things in its servitude, those realizing its needs, neither convince to it to accept its parasites.\nOur scattered sap, our blinded eyes, our vomiting desires, our tongue lies stitched with stain of desires. Desires suggest that",
